1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,840
Hey, you guys.

2
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:12,680
Are we sure this is the right way?

3
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,620
Yep, this is correct.

4
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:17,340
According to our trusty map,

5
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,880
these stairs should lead right to the fifth floor,

6
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:20,880
near the orc settlement.

7
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,280
Seems pretty sketchy.

8
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:27,880
This is amazing.

9
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,100
Look at all these different tentacles.

10
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:33,240
The orcs must have pulled a fast one on us.

11
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,240
There's no way they would leave this be.

12
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:36,020
I don't know.

13
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,420
It does connect to their settlement.

14
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,760
Makes sense they'd want to keep people out.

15
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,440
Let's press on for now.

16
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,640
I think it would save us time and energy

17
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,360
if we just found a different way.

18
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:52,840
Careful.

19
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:55,060
Don't get too close to the wall.

20
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:59,140
These monsters like to hide their bodies inside of them.

21
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:02,800
Lots of tentacles usually means that the walls are hollowed out.

22
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,420
Those things love to set up camp in there.

23
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,440
They interfere with devices,

24
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,960
grow on treasure chests,

25
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:11,380
and are just a general pain in the ass.

26
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,600
I hate them almost as much as I hate mimics.

27
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,880
There.

28
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:19,760
I think we've made very good progress.

29
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:25,320
That's weird.

30
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,100
The orcs should have passed through here

31
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,200
to get to the third floor.

32
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:30,560
But how'd they get through all this?

33
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:32,020
Huh?

34
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,340
Something's here.

35
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:34,240
Be careful.

36
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:34,320
Be careful.

37
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:43,880
Kinsuke!

38
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,480
A giant frog?

39
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,120
A grove!

40
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,100
No!

41
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:49,480
What have you done?

42
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,660
Stand back!

43
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:51,540
Last lap!

44
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:57,900
Hey!

45
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:58,540
Hey!

46
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:01,100
Abrosia!

47
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:01,180
Abrosia!

48
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:01,740
Abrosia!

49
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,320
Abrosia!

50
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:07,880
Abrosia!

51
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:08,320
Abrosia!

52
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,040
Senchi!

53
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:10,800
Behind you!

54
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,280
Don't let go, okay?

55
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:17,760
Do you have a plan?

56
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:20,520
My magic should do the trick!

57
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:20,940
No!

58
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:21,800
We're too close!

59
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,080
This is bad.

60
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:24,620
What should we do?

61
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:26,780
Wait.

62
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,320
That tentacle...

63
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:31,180
There's something about it seems...

64
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:31,980
out of place.

65
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:34,620
I'll bet it's all tangled up in a trap.

66
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:37,960
I wonder if there's any way I could make use of that.

67
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:39,820
But how?

68
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,460
If I touch it directly,

69
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,820
I'll be in for a world of hurt.

70
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:45,960
Huh?

71
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:48,940
Hey, Lyos!

72
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:49,560
Huh?

73
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,960
Why don't the tentacles seem to be hurting the giant frogs at all?

74
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,360
Oh!

75
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:55,300
Uh...

76
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,440
I don't know.

77
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,640
That's just how they're made?

78
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:01,280
Real helpful, Mr. Monsterpedia!

79
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,780
Ah, the curiosity of youth.

80
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:05,780
Ah, whatever.

81
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:11,420
Uh...

82
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:19,320
Wait, what are you doing?

83
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:25,100
It doesn't hurt.

84
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,180
I can do this!

85
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,660
What the...

86
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:31,120
It won't come out!

87
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:37,880
Come on!

88
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,620
Kill Chuck!

89
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:40,040
No!

90
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:40,240
No!

91
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:40,740
No!

92
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:40,840
No!

93
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:41,100
No!

94
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:41,160
No!

95
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:41,220
No!

96
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:51,800
No!

97
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,300
No!

98
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,280
Quick, let's get him out!

99
00:03:58,720 --> 00:03:59,240
Phew!

100
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,120
He's alive.

101
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:00,920
Show me your hands!

102
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:02,280
No way!

103
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,120
They're not hurt?

104
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:04,620
This frogskin,

105
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:07,160
you used it like gloves to protect your hands.

106
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,780
That's really smart.

107
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:13,500
Chill Chuck.

108
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:16,820
This here is a great idea.

109
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:20,440
Start an incision at its belly

110
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:22,740
and completely skin the frog.

111
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,200
Uh, hang on, I...

112
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,900
For the tentacles, peel the skin.

113
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:27,760
Huh?

114
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:29,740
Gather the parts that have thin tips,

115
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:30,680
set them aside,

116
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,540
and boil the thicker parts.

117
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,100
Once done,

118
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,120
mash them up and mix them with flour.

119
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,160
Shape them into cylinders

120
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,960
and gently press with a fork,

121
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:41,920
then boil once more.

122
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:42,620
Tenshi!

123
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:45,120
Hang the skins of the giant frogs to dry,

124
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:46,660
take measurements,

125
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,240
and begin sewing.

126
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:49,600
Add olive oil,

127
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:51,520
garlic and chili peppers,

128
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,620
then the frog leg meat.

129
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:54,900
Fry it all up,

130
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,740
and...

131
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,060
It's ready!

132
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:02,100
I can't believe these guys!

133
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:04,180
Could you both take turns?

134
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,260
Before I could even pick who to stop first,

135
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:07,020
it was too late!

136
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:08,620
Don't be like that.

137
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:09,560
Just try it on.

138
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:10,680
Yes, yes.

139
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:12,480
Come on, go and take a little bite.

140
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:14,520
I told you to take turns!

141
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,360
No way you're getting me to wear that.

142
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,340
If you wore this, Marcille,

143
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:25,040
we think you'd look real cute.

144
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:40,680
It's great, really!

145
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,360
What a nice color on you.

146
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,920
So neat how the eye parts

147
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,300
make it look like we have little ears.

148
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:46,780
Let's go.

149
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,200
Yes, ma'am.

150
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:53,480
Amazing!

151
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:54,900
It doesn't hurt a bit!

152
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,560
This stuff is giving me the heebie-jeebies!

153
00:05:58,220 --> 00:05:59,500
So beautiful.

154
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:01,480
And yummy!

155
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,360
Kensuke!

156
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:09,880
Ambrosia!

157
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:12,880
Guys?

158
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,380
The castle town.

159
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,940
We're already on the fifth floor.

160
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:24,760
Looks like they left in a hurry.

161
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:27,980
So the orcs were telling the truth then.

162
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:31,560
And that means the red dragon can't be far off.

163
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:33,160
Let's stay on our guard

164
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,540
and see what else we can find here.

165
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:35,600
Right.

166
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:37,760
Hey, uh...

167
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,660
Laios?

168
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:41,680
Is this frog blood?

169
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:43,500
It hardened onto my clothes

170
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,500
and now I can't get this thing off of me.

171
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,960
It's because I didn't really have the time

172
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,100
to completely tan it.

173
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:51,800
We're fighting the dragon like this?

174
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,740
Forget the dragon!

175
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:58,400
How am I going to look felon in the eyes, huh?

176
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,220
Answer me!

177
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:17,240
My insides don't feel so good.

178
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:20,120
Kiki, Kaka, show Namari to the guest room.

179
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:25,460
While you do that, I will go and report to the island lord.

180
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:35,160
So, how was the dungeon?

181
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:40,700
The thing to be most concerned about is it has become more perilous.

182
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:44,400
Treasure down to the third floor has been stripped bare.

183
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,940
Hideouts for outlaws are on the rise.

184
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,540
And orcs have been appearing on the upper floors

185
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:53,440
and are frequently causing problems.

186
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:56,240
I would suggest sending in troops

187
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,820
or offering a bounty.

188
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:02,080
How do they even manage to find their way in?

189
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:05,820
Perhaps the pathways were connected from old dwarven tunnels.

190
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,120
Orcs have been known to settle in such places.

191
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,480
Dwarves, you say?

192
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,820
What a truly troublesome lot they are.

193
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,760
They're like moles.

194
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:17,640
No matter how many holes we close, another pops up.

195
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,900
Long ago, when the elves and dwarves split

196
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,040
between east and west because of a war,

197
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,400
the dwarves hid in these lands,

198
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,360
waiting for the elves to attack.

199
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,480
Even after the war ended,

200
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,400
they continued digging holes,

201
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:34,580
eventually turning the golden country into a dungeon.

202
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:38,080
I've even heard that the dungeon continues to grow

203
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:40,740
because of the descendants of those very dwarves.

204
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:44,060
Let us move on from unsubstantiated rumors.

205
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,840
Here are the drawings of the magic circles.

206
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:50,020
They are in the usual eldish language.

207
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:51,720
And according to the penmanship,

208
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,160
it is the same author.

209
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,700
And there are no signs of anyone else

210
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,060
modifying them at all.

211
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,440
There's no mistaking it.

212
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:00,780
The lord of the dungeon,

213
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:02,600
or should I say the mad mage,

214
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:04,080
drew these magic circles.

215
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,420
Is this individual an elf?

216
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,300
I cannot say with certainty,

217
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:11,580
but it's unlikely a tall man or dwarf cast it.

218
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,040
This is concerning.

219
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:14,060
Hmm?

220
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,020
The thing is, the other day,

221
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:18,740
I received a letter from the elves of the west.

222
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:19,840
It said,

223
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,880
the dungeon belongs to us.

224
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:23,200
Relinquish it.

225
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,860
How utterly conceited!

226
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:28,120
They're the ones who gave the lands to the humans

227
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:31,680
after taking and squandering those lands from the dwarves.

228
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,160
Just ignore them.

229
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:36,220
This land was bestowed to me by the king of the elves,

230
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:38,060
so I'm afraid that's not possible.

231
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:39,200
Hmm.

232
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,920
Now take the entire island.

233
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:44,120
I certainly hope not.

234
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,820
There is most likely a vast amount of riches

235
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,600
still in the bowels of that dungeon.

236
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:49,540
My lord,

237
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:52,580
their objective is not any material treasure,

238
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:55,840
but the immortality spell cast on the dungeon.

239
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:58,680
This spell that tethers the soul to the body

240
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,020
is still a great mystery.

241
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,740
And once that mystery becomes unraveled,

242
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:05,620
its value will far exceed any amount of gold.

243
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:08,400
We should solve it before the elves do.

244
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:12,000
So we should trace all of the magic circles and study them?

245
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:13,580
That's not enough!

246
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:17,160
A powerful spell such as this is bound to have a schematic.

247
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,960
You should seek it out.

248
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:21,540
After we get our hands on it,

249
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,940
then you can agree to give them back the dungeon.

250
00:10:24,940 --> 00:10:28,000
Once they realize we possess that valuable knowledge,

251
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,140
the elves will see you as an equal.

252
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:30,900
No.

253
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:34,360
They will kneel before you to curry your favor.

254
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,660
You... you think so?

255
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:39,140
So where do you think it might be?

256
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:41,200
Isn't it obvious?

257
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:44,600
The lord of the dungeon would have possession over it.

258
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:47,920
So we should keep sending in adventurers to search the premises?

259
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,260
That is correct.

260
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:53,720
Monster extermination and buying artifacts from the dungeon is pivotal.

261
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:57,260
Spend your coin and aid those adventurers.

262
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:58,800
I understand.

263
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,420
I will put out a reward for the orcs.

264
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:03,460
And my reply to the elves?

265
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:06,220
I will pen something that buys us some time.

266
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,320
Laios was his name, yes.

267
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:13,180
He was quite the skilled adventurer.

268
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:16,200
But I wonder just how far he will go.

269
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:23,940
Good morning, Namaari.

270
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,240
How are you feeling?

271
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:27,600
Wait!

272
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,080
Where's my ex?

273
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,060
Your stuff is there.

274
00:11:31,980 --> 00:11:34,640
Also, this is from Grandpa Tonsu.

275
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,840
Isn't this too much?

276
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,760
You can think of it as a retainer.

277
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,640
For when he needs you in the future.

278
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,380
Oh, thanks a lot.

279
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:46,240
I appreciate it.

280
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,160
Do you need a town guide?

281
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:52,980
So, where are you staying?

282
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:54,840
You must be going to rest up.

283
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:55,860
Not yet.

284
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,480
I'm going back to the dungeon.

285
00:11:58,540 --> 00:11:59,380
Oh, my.

286
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:00,860
You're returning already?

287
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:01,800
No, no.

288
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:04,020
I just have some business at the temple nearby.

289
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:06,020
Business?

290
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:07,020
Business.

291
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:08,020
Revivals.

292
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:17,680
Revivals.

293
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:18,940
Huh?

294
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:20,320
Oh, Namaari.

295
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:23,600
Those are the eyes of someone looking for something.

296
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:27,800
So, is it a thing or a person?

297
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:28,700
Person.

298
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:30,440
A female tall man.

299
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,520
Hair light brown.

300
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,660
Length would be about down to the shoulders.

301
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,600
Her age is...

302
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,860
somewhere from teens to forties.

303
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:39,660
Hang on.

304
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,240
Is this Laios' sister?

305
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:44,200
There's no question that girl is in her twenties.

306
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,060
Go get your eyes checked out.

307
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:47,500
Give me a break.

308
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,060
How should I know, huh?

309
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,320
Hmm.

310
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,720
Nothing by that description has been brought here yet.

311
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,200
I see.

312
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:58,920
The fifth floor.

313
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:03,120
Exiting the Golden Castle leads to the castle town.

314
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:07,440
The area has expanded and distorted due to magic.

315
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:10,940
But you can still sense phantoms of its former glory.

316
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:14,840
A person passing by, just out of sight.

317
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,400
The sound of someone whispering.

318
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,160
These strange feelings linger like a dream.

319
00:13:23,780 --> 00:13:26,360
So this is where the orcs set up their post.

320
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,080
Looks like they left here in a hurry, too.

321
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,360
Their food storage is a complete mess.

322
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,340
What a horrible smell.

323
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,880
Must have been ransacked by nearby monsters.

324
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:38,760
Looks like the flour and alcohol are okay.

325
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:39,820
Oh.

326
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,660
Let's bake some bread.

327
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:44,140
If the orcs come back, they'll be mad.

328
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,520
Ah, we gave them vegetables, so we should be squared away.

329
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:47,800
Okay.

330
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:01,220
Wargs.

331
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,380
Was this the red dragon?

332
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:05,700
Seems so.

333
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:08,360
Looks like they all got hit by its fire-breath attack.

334
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,200
Going by the smoke.

335
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:13,240
It must have just been here.

336
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,260
Hey, Laios.

337
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:20,360
I remember you saying that dragons aren't really active, that they mostly sleep a lot.

338
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:28,940
But going off what the orcs said and seeing all this, it's been moving around ever since, and might even be wandering around nearby.

339
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:35,420
I think we could have won against a sleeping dragon, but can we really defeat it now?

340
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:40,420
What if we lose, or what if she's already been digested?

341
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:44,680
Hey, it's all right. Take a deep breath. Let's just think it all through.

342
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:49,480
Well, whatever you decide, don't forget you'll have to fight it with just three people.

343
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,020
Just three?

344
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:57,220
Don't look at me like that! I told you that I'm not built for fighting!

345
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,520
My job was to help get all of you here, and that's all!

346
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:01,540
We know that.

347
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,160
We weren't blaming you.

348
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,660
I may have overreacted.

349
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:08,820
So how are you defeating dragons before now?

350
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:12,840
Well, it depended on a bunch of different factors, but...

351
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:15,080
Fallon would cast protection spells against fire.

352
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:18,140
Namari, Shuro, and I would slow its movement.

353
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:20,960
Marcil would weaken it with explosion magic.

354
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,540
And Shuro would deliver the final blow.

355
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:26,680
I think that's how it would go, at least.

356
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:30,560
But that's not gonna work with the party we have now, though.

357
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:33,960
We have to think of a plan that'll work for the three of us.

358
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:40,180
Dragons are covered in super-tough scales, making them resistant to magic and weapons.

359
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:45,420
But under its neck, there's an inverse scale that serves as its weak spot.

360
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,640
If we strike there, we can win.

361
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,160
Under the neck?

362
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:52,800
And about how big would you say this red dragon is, exactly?

363
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,800
How to explain...

364
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,280
Oh! See that there?

365
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:59,480
It's about as tall as that crumbled passageway.

366
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:04,200
I mean, that literally looks like the dragon bonked its head there.

367
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:05,960
Oh, that makes sense.

368
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:07,860
It's quite huge.

369
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:11,160
It'll be no easy task, striking the scale from that height.

370
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,800
Yeah, you are not kidding.

371
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:14,380
Hmm.

372
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,640
Let's try getting up there.

373
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:20,780
It's pretty high up.

374
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:23,460
What if we jumped on the dragon's neck from here?

375
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,520
You can't do that!

376
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:25,340
What she said.

377
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:29,780
I can cast Abjuration Spells, but they won't be as good as Falon's.

378
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:34,300
If you fall from this height, you'll definitely hurt yourself, and it'll all be over.

379
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,740
And that's not all.

380
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:37,160
What about its fire breath?

381
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:38,960
None of us can outrun that.

382
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:39,880
Oh, yeah.

383
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:43,860
Namaari also said that Senshi's axe won't stand a chance against it.

384
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,840
What about your weapon, Laios?

385
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:50,440
You'd have to keep it occupied while I'm charging up a strong explosion spell.

386
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:52,180
One that will knock it unconscious.

387
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,760
And after that, someone will have to fatally wound it.

388
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:58,740
Do you think you and Senshi can pull all of that off?

389
00:16:59,200 --> 00:16:59,840
Of course.

390
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:01,280
I'm sure we can.

391
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:02,340
Okay, how?

392
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:04,140
Oh.

393
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:09,840
Instead of hitting the dragon, what if we were to blow up a structure instead?

394
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:14,060
There are lots of houses and bridges that extend between buildings.

395
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:20,200
We blow one up when the dragon goes and walks under it, and the rubble should slow down its movement.

396
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:25,300
With all that rubble weighing it down, the inverse scale will be within striking distance.

397
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:29,740
We won't be able to buy much time when we're actually fighting it.

398
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:33,820
But we can lure it somewhere we want while we're running away from it.

399
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:36,280
These paths are narrow for a red dragon.

400
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:39,620
It should also be tired from being so active.

401
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:43,360
With the proper route, we can tire it out even more.

402
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:44,620
I see.

403
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,740
Well, I can probably help with that, then.

404
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:47,400
Really?

405
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:49,140
Thank you, too, Doug.

406
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,060
I'm so happy!

407
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:52,980
I wonder why the dragon's not sleeping, though.

408
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:55,400
And why'd it show up on Floor 5?

409
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:58,880
It seems to be wandering around narrow areas that it doesn't like.

410
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,660
Maybe it's mating time?

411
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:01,820
Probably not.

412
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,240
Oh, hang on a sec.

413
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:06,820
Didn't Amari say Senshi's pen is made out of a really cool metal?

414
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:07,800
What was it?

415
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:11,620
Something about blocking the dragon's fangs and smashing through its bones, I think?

416
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:12,140
Oh!

417
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,380
That's right!

418
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,660
She said that blacksmiths dream about this stuff!

419
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:18,800
If that's true, it must be able to block its fire breath.

420
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:19,540
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

421
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:22,260
Well, that's one of our problems taken care of.

422
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:25,120
Sure, that knife isn't also made from something special.

423
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:27,920
We should have had Amari look at it, huh?

424
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:30,580
I'm starting to feel like we can do this.

425
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:33,220
Like they say, if there's a will, there's a way.

426
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:33,900
Right.

427
00:18:34,340 --> 00:18:36,180
Let's finish planning out our attack.

428
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:56,720
Oh, you're back.

429
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:58,900
Senshi, why did you wander off?

430
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,200
We were wondering where you went.

431
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,600
I was making bread.

432
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:04,480
You know we're about to fight a dragon, don't you?

433
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:05,600
Of course.

434
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:08,040
This will be quite the task, don't you think?

435
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,440
A good meal is most important.

436
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:15,360
We've already lost once to this dragon because of an empty stomach.

437
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:17,440
This time will be different.

438
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:18,200
Right?

439
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:20,080
There's wine!

440
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:23,120
I went and borrowed a few things from the pantry.

441
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:26,680
Not until we beat the dragon.

442
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:30,780
We don't have any eggs, but we should still be able to make that.

443
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,140
Shave down some bread with a grater.

444
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:38,740
Season the giant frog meat with salt and pepper.

445
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:42,000
Dip the meat in a water and flour mixture.

446
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,820
Work in the breadcrumbs.

447
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:46,600
Then heat some olive oil and fry.

448
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:53,060
Boil down some bread, wine, and seasonings to make a sauce.

449
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:57,720
It's ready.

450
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:01,580
Looks delicious.

451
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:04,680
Once I started smelling it, I got really hungry.

452
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,280
Let's do it again, everyone!

453
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:09,680
It's so crispy.

454
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,660
What's wrong, Marcel?

455
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:19,480
Knowing these monster meals will come to an end soon just got me a little emotional.

456
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:21,760
Well, let's not get ahead of ourselves.

457
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,660
Everyone, I want to say something.

458
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:33,880
I don't think I would have been able to make it this far on my own.

459
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:36,340
Senshi, thank you.

460
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:39,780
We were strangers, but you were still kind to us.

461
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:43,860
Your food not only filled our stomachs, but my heart as well.

462
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:49,640
Chilchuk, if you weren't with us, we would have lost days taking the long way down.

463
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,380
That helped us so much.

464
00:20:52,340 --> 00:20:56,260
And Marcel, I'm sorry for putting you through everything.

465
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:59,740
When you said you'd come with us, I was really happy.

466
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:03,620
Everyone, thank you so much.

467
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:08,640
Of course!

468
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,080
You're so cringe!

469
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:10,880
Sorry.

470
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:35,940
It's even bigger than I remembered it being.

471
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:37,140
No kidding.

472
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:38,980
Can we really defeat that?

473
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:40,200
What?

474
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:41,720
We'll be fine.

475
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:43,720
We all got this far, didn't we?

476
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:45,820
Let's review the plan.

477
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:49,620
Marcel has her spot, which we'll lure the dragon to.

478
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:51,460
Is everyone ready?

479
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:54,100
Seems our health is in good shape.

480
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:55,900
All right.

481
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:57,980
Let's go!

